  "name": "Question 4",
  "problem": "Which of the following is equivalent to  $\\operatorname{tanh}\u2061(\\frac{1}{t}),$ for $t\\ne 0?$",
  "worked_solution": "The definition of $\\operatorname{tanh}\u2061x$ is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{tanh}\u2061x & =\\frac{{e}^{x}-{e}^{-x}}{{e}^{x}+{e}^{-x}} \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{2x}-1}{{e}^{2x}+1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1-{e}^{-2x}}{1+{e}^{-2x}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the second definition, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{tanh}\u2061(\\frac{1}{t}) & =\\frac{{e}^{2(1/t)}-1}{{e}^{2(1/t)}+1} \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{2/t}-1}{{e}^{2/t}+1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
